{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-237281",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=5x$ and $b=\\sqrt{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-\\sqrt{6})(5x+\\sqrt{6}) & = \\\\ (5x)^{2}-(\\sqrt{6})^{2} & = \\\\ 25{x}^{2}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
